    "title": "Wembanyama Leads Spurs to Victory Over Rockets",
    "text": "• The San Antonio Spurs defeated the Houston Rockets 111-99.\n• Victor Wembanyama scored 28 points, had 16 rebounds, and 5 blocks for the Spurs.\n• The Spurs trailed by 16 points at one point in the game.\n• The Spurs took the lead late in the third quarter.\n• Wembanyama scored 9 points in an 11-0 run to start the fourth quarter.\n• Dylan Harper scored 6 points in a 10-4 run for the Spurs.\n• Amen Thompson scored 25 points for the Rockets.\n• Kevin Durant scored 24 points for the Rockets.\n• Alperen Sengun had 18 points, 10 rebounds, and 7 assists for the Rockets.\n• The Spurs shot 53.7% from the field.\n• The Rockets shot 39.4% from the field.\n• The Spurs now lead the season series 2-1.\n• The Spurs play at Charlotte on Saturday.\n• The Rockets play at Atlanta on Thursday.",
    "summary": "Wembanyama scored nine points, with five free throws, to power an 11-0 run to open the fourth quarter that put the Spurs on top 95-86 with less than eight minutes to go. A pair of free throws by Alperen Sengun got the Rockets within five before San Antonio used a 10-4 run, with six points from Dylan Harper, to make it 107-96 with about 2 1/2 minutes to play. Wembanyama’s big game comes after he was 5 of 21 for 14 points in a loss to Houston last week.",
